cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PurRDF, please cite it as below."
title: "PurRDF — the RDF 1.2 toolkit with a purr"
abstract: >-
  PurRDF is a from-scratch, dependency-light Rust toolkit for RDF 1.2 that carries one
  engine — and one behavior — into Rust, Python, WebAssembly/JavaScript, and C. It
  provides an immutable, value-interned RDF 1.2 dataset IR (triple terms, reifiers,
  base-direction literals); first-party codecs for Turtle, TriG, N-Triples, N-Quads,
  RDF/XML, TriX, HexTuples, JSON-LD, and YAML-LD with one RFC 3986 base-resolution
  layer; W3C RDFC-1.0 dataset canonicalization; a native SPARQL 1.1/1.2 parser,
  algebra, and multiset evaluator with governed execution, SEP-0009 composite
  datatypes, and SPARQL Results JSON/XML/CSV/TSV; SHACL validation (Core,
  SHACL-SPARQL, and SHACL-AF including SHACL Rules); ShEx 2.1 validation;
  entailment regimes (RDF, RDFS, OWL 2 RL, D, an OWL 2 Direct-Semantics
  tableau, and RIF-Core) that return a reasoning report with every closure;
  deterministic full-text search with exact fixed-point BM25 ranking; exact,
  float-free GeoSPARQL 1.1; embedding nearest-neighbour search over the PURREMB
  companion format; and the GTS single-file, content-addressed, append-only graph
  transport. Together, the full-text, GeoSPARQL and nearest-neighbour surfaces
  answer from SPARQL, in-process and over one dataset, the three queries for
  which an RDF project has usually run PostgreSQL beside its triple store, with
  the same result natively and on WebAssembly. The workspace deliberately exposes no optional Cargo features — as a
  data carrier it guarantees byte-identical semantics for every consumer — and
  its behavior is gated by W3C SPARQL, SHACL, shexTest, OWL 2, RDFC-1.0, and
  frozen cross-language GTS conformance corpora.
